          "settings": {
            "question": "Can the glass railing on my canal-lot pool deck serve as the pool barrier?",
            "answer": "<p>The Residential Swimming Pool Safety Act sets the barrier at least 48 inches high on the outside, with gates that close on their own and open away from the pool. A 48-inch glass fence on 46-inch panels, with gate hinges, a latch and a floor lock, is built to those heights. Whether it counts as the barrier for your lot, including the seawall side, is the building department's call, so ask before ordering.</p>",
