            "question": "Do A1A condo balconies need a top rail on the glass?",
            "answer": "<p>Ask the building department and the association before you order. Condos fall under the building volume of the Florida Building Code, where guards are 42 inches, and a reviewer may ask for a top rail on glass guards in a multifamily building. Our square caprail is made for the 12 mm panels and comes in both finishes. Without it, the frameless look stays as it is: panels in spigots, no posts.</p>",
            "pages": ""
